       turnState?: "ready" | "waiting" | "enemy" | "locked" | "over";
       ```
     - In `Board` (`apps/web/src/game/Board.tsx:632-633`), compute `endTurnState` as `"over"` whenever `view.result !== null`:
       ```typescript
       const ownTurn = view.result === null && view.active === view.viewer;
       const endTurnState =
         view.result !== null ? "over" : !ownTurn ? "enemy" : !endTurnLegal ? "locked" : actionsRemain ? "ready" : "waiting";
       ```
     - In `Board`'s `<ControlButton control="end-turn" ...>` (`apps/web/src/game/Board.tsx:822`), update the `label` prop:
       ```typescript
       label={
         endTurnState === "over"
           ? t("Game over")
           : endTurnState === "enemy"
             ? t("Enemy turn")
             : armed
               ? t("Confirm end turn")
               : (endTurnLabel ?? t("End turn"))
       }
       ```
       (Note: `t("Game over")` already exists in `apps/web/src/i18n/zh-CN.json`).
   - In `apps/web/src/game/board.css`:
     - At line 2623, extend the selector beside `[data-turn-state="enemy"]`:
